From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Grische <github@grische.xyz>
Date: Wed, 19 Aug 2026 13:01:58 +0200
Subject: leds: lgm-sso: do not free a regmap owned by syscon

The driver gets its regmap from syscon_node_to_regmap() and then calls
regmap_exit() on it in both probe error paths and again in .remove.
The regmap is not the driver's to free.

syscon_node_to_regmap() either returns an existing entry or creates one
with of_syscon_register(), which puts it on the global syscon_list
(drivers/mfd/syscon.c, list_add_tail() at the end of the function).
Nothing in that file ever takes an entry off that list again -- there
is no list_del() in it at all -- and the list is keyed by device_node,
so the regmap outlives every consumer by design and the next lookup of
the same node hands out the same pointer.

Freeing it therefore leaves a dangling entry on syscon_list. The next
caller gets a pointer to freed memory, and that caller can be this same
driver: both probe error paths are reachable with -EPROBE_DEFER
underneath them, the sole gpiod get in sso_led_dt_parse() being the
obvious source, so a deferred probe frees the regmap and the retry then
uses it. The driver can also be built as a module, which puts .remove
on the same footing.

Drop all three calls. The regmap needs no teardown here: syscon owns
it, and on the error paths there is nothing else left to undo -- the
clocks are released by the devm action registered above them.

Fixes: c3987cd2bca3 ("leds: lgm: Add LED controller driver for LGM SoC")
Assisted-by: Claude:claude-fable-5
Signed-off-by: Grische <github@grische.xyz>

diff --git a/drivers/leds/blink/leds-lgm-sso.c b/drivers/leds/blink/leds-lgm-sso.c
index 62a573637bd9..96e327ca5d55 100644
--- a/drivers/leds/blink/leds-lgm-sso.c
+++ b/drivers/leds/blink/leds-lgm-sso.c
@@ -815,10 +815,8 @@ static int intel_sso_led_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 	}
 
 	ret = sso_probe_gpios(priv);
-	if (ret) {
-		regmap_exit(priv->mmap);
+	if (ret)
 		return ret;
-	}
 
 	INIT_LIST_HEAD(&priv->led_list);
 
@@ -828,10 +826,9 @@ static int intel_sso_led_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 	priv->gptc_clkrate = DEF_GPTC_CLK_RATE;
 
 	ret = sso_led_dt_parse(priv);
-	if (ret) {
-		regmap_exit(priv->mmap);
+	if (ret)
 		return ret;
-	}
+
 	dev_info(priv->dev, "sso LED init success!\n");
 
 	return 0;
@@ -848,8 +845,6 @@ static void intel_sso_led_remove(struct platform_device *pdev)
 		list_del(&led->list);
 		sso_led_shutdown(led);
 	}
-
-	regmap_exit(priv->mmap);
 }
 
